---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="OneDrive for TwineLine"
  description="OneDrive storage options and pricing for use with TwineLine."
>
  <div
    class="content-pane mx-auto max-w-4xl mt-0 md:mt-10 mb-0 md:mb-20 px-4 md:px-10 py-6 md:py-12 rounded-none md:rounded-2xl border-0 md:border"
    style="--tw-border-opacity:1; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);"
  >
    <section class="py-3 sm:py-5">
      <h1
        class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-tight mb-4"
        style="color: var(--text-primary);"
      >
        OneDrive for TwineLine
      </h1>

      <p
        class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4"
        style="color: var(--text-secondary);"
      >
        TwineLine uses Microsoft OneDrive to store and access your photos and
        videos. OneDrive provides the best cross-platform access of any major
        cloud storage provider, which is why TwineLine relies on it.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold mb-3 mt-6"
        style="color: var(--text-primary);"
      >
        Storage options
      </h2>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table
          class="w-full text-sm sm:text-base"
          style="color: var(--text-secondary);"
        >
          <thead>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
              <th
                class="text-left py-2 pr-4 font-semibold"
                style="color: var(--text-primary);">Plan</th
              >
              <th
                class="text-left py-2 pr-4 font-semibold"
                style="color: var(--text-primary);">Storage</th
              >
              <th
                class="text-left py-2 pr-4 font-semibold"
                style="color: var(--text-primary);">Price</th
              >
              <th
                class="text-left py-2 font-semibold"
                style="color: var(--text-primary);">Notes</th
              >
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">OneDrive Basic</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">5 GB</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Free</td>
              <td class="py-2"
                >Good for trying TwineLine with a small collection</td
              >
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Microsoft 365 Basic</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">100 GB</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">$1.99/mo</td>
              <td class="py-2">Suitable for moderate collections</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--glass-border);">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Microsoft 365 Personal</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">1 TB</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">$8.99/mo*</td>
              <td class="py-2"
                >Includes Office apps; recommended for large collections</td
              >
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Microsoft 365 Family</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">6 TB</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">$12.99/mo*</td>
              <td class="py-2">Up to 6 people, 1 TB each</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-2" style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8rem;">
        *Paid annually. Monthly billing is slightly higher.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold mb-3 mt-6"
        style="color: var(--text-primary);"
      >
        How much storage do I need?
      </h2>
      <p
        class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4"
        style="color: var(--text-secondary);"
      >
        A typical phone photo is about 3&ndash;5 MB. A collection of 10,000
        photos would need roughly 30&ndash;50 GB of storage. Videos take
        significantly more space. If you have a large collection with lots of
        video, the 1 TB plan is the best value.
      </p>

      <h2
        class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold mb-3 mt-6"
        style="color: var(--text-primary);"
      >
        Why not Google Drive or iCloud?
      </h2>
      <p
        class="text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4"
        style="color: var(--text-secondary);"
      >
        Google closed third-party API access to Google Photos in 2025.
        Apple&rsquo;s iCloud Photos API is only available on Apple devices.
        Microsoft OneDrive is the only major provider that offers full,
        cross-platform API access to photos and their metadata (including
        location data), which TwineLine needs to create intelligent slideshows.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-6">
        <a
          href="/how-it-works"
          class="nav-link text-sm"
          style="color: var(--accent);">&larr; Back to How it works</a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
